Cell[BoxData["\<\"05_conditioning_noise_sensitivity.nb \
completed.\\n\\nPurpose:\\nValidate conditioning dependence of the polar \
holonomy estimator under noisy overlap matrices.\\n\\nBaseline:\\nRank-2 \
tangent-frame loop with N_base = 80.\\nBase minimum singular value = \
0.998721.\\n\\nControlled conditioning construction:\\nEach clean overlap is \
replaced by polar(M_k) . DiagonalMatrix[{1, mu}], so the polar factor is \
unchanged while the smallest singular value is controlled.\\n\\nScaled-noise \
test:\\neta = rho * mu_min.\\nExpected behavior: mean holonomy error scales \
approximately linearly with rho = eta/mu_min for small \
perturbations.\\n\\nFixed-eta test:\\neta =    \
1\\n-------\\n1000000.\\nExpected behavior: mean holonomy error increases as \
mu_min decreases.\\n\\nTrials per point:\\n20\\n\\nScaled-noise slope \
table:\\n{{0.95, 0.9499999999999997, 0.994712640503972, 0.994712640503972}, \
{0.7, 0.7, 1.0174542133178999, 1.0174542133178999}, {0.5, 0.4999999999999999, \
0.9469789208636373, 0.9469789208636373}, {0.3, 0.29999999999999993, \
1.0660735082528079, 1.0660735082528079}, {0.15, 0.15, 0.9827462579908893, \
0.9827462579908893}}\\n\\nFixed-eta fit summary:\\n<|\\\"fixed_eta\\\" -> \
1/1000000, \\\"log_log_slope_error_vs_inverse_mu\\\" -> \
0.3644515184119498|>\\n\\nBase diagnostics:\\n<|\\\"n_base\\\" -> 80, \
\\\"base_min_singular_value\\\" -> 0.9987206428555113, \
\\\"base_unitarity_error\\\" -> 8.018071306342336*^-15, \
\\\"base_eigenphases\\\" -> {-1.4765148199856373, 1.4765148199856373}, \
\\\"base_wilson_traces_r1_r2_r3\\\" -> {0.18828378156806824, \
-1.9645492175984391, -0.558176537334093}|>\\n\\nGenerated \
